WEBVTT

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
bokura nara daijoubu

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
Because we’re still doing okay,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
we can become even stronger!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
takaihiroi sora megake

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
Aiming for the tall and wide sky,

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
kinou made no boku wo hanatsu

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
I let go of what I was up until yesterday.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
miesuita uso mo, taikutsu na

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
Those lies that were easily seen through and my tedious day-by-day life;

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
hibi mo, zenbu hodoite

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
I left them both behind.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
atarashii asa ni me wo hosome

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
I narrowed my eyes at the new morning

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
kyou mo bokutachi wa ikiteku

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
Today we shall also venture out
to live our lives again.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
sukoshi nami utsu sabishisadatte

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
Even the slight loneliness that sometimes comes about,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
taisetsu ni omoeteru

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
I consider important.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
itsuka kanjita shinjitsu mo

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
Even the truth I felt some day…

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
massugu koko kara asu ni mukatteru

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
…is urging us to go on into the future.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
bokutachi ga mezashita sekai

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
The world that we had all aimed for…

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
donna kakomo kakaeta mama kitto tadoritsuku

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
We will arrive at it, no matter what our pasts are.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.460
fumidashita kewashii michi mo

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.460
We continued forward, even if it is a steep path…

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.900
bokura nara daijoubu,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.900
…because we’re still doing okay,

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
and we can become even stronger!

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:43.250
Ah, we’re going to be late!

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:46.750
Please hurry, we mustn’t keep Nozomu-kun waiting.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:50.960
It’s tight, but I will endure it!

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.410
Nozomu-kun’s going to see it.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:59.880
Misses, it’s almost time.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.390
I am deeply sorry! I thought that you were done.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:04.600
It’s all right.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.520
Please wait a little bit more.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.740
How beautiful you are!

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:23.060
If the master could see you, he would be so happy.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:26.290
Hatsumoude: a custom where people visit a temple or shrine in the first few days of the new year to pray.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:27.690
I’m off.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:35.290
Ever since I met Kira-chan and Yura-chan on Christmas Eve,

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:42.090
I haven’t seen Kaoruko-chan or Sumireko-chan.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:50.790
For some reason, I can’t get Kaoruko-chan’s face from that moment out of my mind.

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:02.940
I wonder if he’s here yet…

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.490
Ah! There he is!

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:12.330
Nozomu-kun!

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.230
Nozomu-kun?

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:28.230
Oh, yeah…

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:33.020
Happy New Year.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.270
Happy New Year.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.770
What’s the matter, Nozomu-kun? You’re acting strangely today.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.740
Yes indeed, strangely!

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:45.830
Is that so? You two are just so beautiful…

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.840
Kira-chan and Yura-chan, you two are so beautiful that you just took me by surprise.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:57.370
I’m so happy!

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.340
Thank you very much, Nozomu-kun.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.630
It wasn’t a bother, was it? Inviting you so openly…

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:11.180
No, not really. I don’t really have anywhere else to go.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:16.440
Somehow, we both earnestly wanted to visit the shrine with you, Nozomu-kun.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:20.360
So that we could pray for passing the exams and getting into the same high school.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.570
Yeah, it would be great to go to the same high school, although–

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.060
That’s no good!

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:28.110
Right! If we’re not together, it’s no good at all!

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:29.860
Ah, okay.

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:33.120
We couldn’t imagine going to a different school, Nozomu-kun.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.160
We want to be together with you forever, right, Yura-chan?

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:37.340
Yes, Kira-chan.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.360
I pray that we can go to the same high school.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:58.770
Please, let us go to the same high school as Nozomu-kun.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:01.320
Please, let us be with Nozomu-kun.

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:06.870
Kira-chan and Yura-chan… they’re really good girls, aren’t they?

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:12.040
For them to think this much of me,
I guess I have a reason to be happy.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:17.920
Nozomu-kun?

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:24.730
So Ruru-chan and Rara-chan are helping out here?

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:25.630
Where? Where?

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:31.830
Umm, I believe at the oracle stand near the entrance. Oh, over there!

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.310
Kaoruko-chan?

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:36.900
Were you waiting?

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:37.900
You’re late.

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:42.250
That’s not her. What am I so worried about?

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:45.880
Being seen with Kira-chan and Yura-chan is none of their concern…

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:49.910
Still, perhaps Kaoruko-chan and Sumireko-chan are visiting the temple?

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:57.320
Nozomu-oniichan!

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:58.580
Over here, over here!

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:06.050
You sure look good in those.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:07.620
You’re so cute!

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:10.110
You’re helping out here? How admirable.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.270
We’re doing a part time job.

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:14.430
We’re getting a lot of candy.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:18.690
Is that so? So can we go straight to drawing our fortunes?

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:19.850
Me too.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:20.810
And me too.

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:23.650
No. 32.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.400
Here you go.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.430
Okay, thank you.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:29.400
So this is it?

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:30.120
Yes.

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:33.370
The two of us got “a little bit of good luck”.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:36.870
Even your fortunes are identical.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:40.910
It says that overall, and especially with math studies, things will be good.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:43.590
What’s the matter?

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:47.300
“A great obstacle is in the way of romance.”

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:51.260
Mine says that my springtime is still far away.

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:51.260
Springtime refers to romance in Japanese literary conventions.

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:53.650
It’s nothing to be concerned about.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:57.010
There are times when the oracles are right and times when they’re wrong.

00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:01.940
It doesn’t say you two will never find love. You can always overcome the obstacles.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:04.400
And spring will always come.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.270
Thank you very much, Nozomu-kun.

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:11.160
The way you said that – for some reason, I feel a lot better.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:12.010
Yup.

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:14.270
Now let’s see mine…

00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:20.620
Plain lucky?

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:24.370
I guess that’s fine, being lucky.
That’s about normal then, huh?

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:28.180
Just a little below
“a little bit of good luck.”

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.920
Is that so?

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:32.400
Overall, you’ll do well within your limits.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:34.590
If you push hard in school, you’ll do fine for yourself.

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:38.280
Ambiguity in love will lead to punishment?

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:39.920
It seems this reading is pretty accurate.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:41.190
It is just a fortune drawing.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:43.860
Yes. Sometimes it’s correct, sometimes it’s not.

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:45.810
I guess so.

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:51.780
Ah, the Ichijou sisters!

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:59.000
Yuuya, Kaoruko-chan.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:06.340
Oh, it was the three of them.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:10.050
Nozomu-chan! The Sakurazuki-sans!

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:12.530
What wonderful, fine clothing!

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:13.930
You too, Ichijou-sans.

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:16.260
What’s up.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.110
Hey.

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:18.950
New Year’s Temple visit with the Sakurazukis, huh?

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:20.090
Way to go, Nozomu.

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:21.600
Oh, it’s nothing like that.

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:23.560
Sumireko…

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.440
Hey, they’re pounding mochi over there!

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:29.700
Mochi: Sticky rice cakes, a traditional New Year’s food.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:29.700
Like mushroom-shaped mochi and dark sugar mochi and many others!

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:30.820
Let’s go! Let’s go!

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.420
Wow, let’s go.

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:33.700
Let’s go, let’s go.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.900
Come on, hurry!

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:49.130
Hey. You know, I did confess to Kaoruko-chan.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:51.840
Ah, yes.

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:56.430
Kaoruko-chan told me…

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:59.120
I know already, don’t bother, I know.

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:00.230
I see.

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:02.750
You don’t need to go to these lengths to tell me.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:04.270
It has nothing to do with me.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:07.080
Yeah, I suppose that’s true.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:13.820
But since she’s studying for entrance exams, going out with her is still wishful thinking.

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:15.020
Yeah.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:20.260
I’m confident! I’ll have Kaoruko-chan fall more and more in love with me.

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:21.290
Or something like that.

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:27.330
Gonda?

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.210
Don’t get too close to the Ichijou sisters!

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:34.380
Your being around them is a distraction from their entrance exam studies.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.300
Friends of yours?

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.930
Yeah, Gonda and his friends
are from school.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:41.170
They’re like Kaoruku-chan and Sumireko-chan’s fan club.

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:42.760
I see.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:45.440
You people have no right to say anything like that to me.

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:48.200
I will see Kaoruko-chan and Sumireko-chan when I want to see them.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:48.690
That’s all there is to it.

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:49.920
What did you just say?!

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:50.650
Back off.

00:09:51.030 --> 00:09:53.320
So you’re saying you’re not going to listen to me?

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:54.360
Yes.

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:57.890
If that’s your attitude, then I challenge you.

00:09:57.890 --> 00:10:02.540
If you lose, you will clearly distance yourself from the Ichijous.

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:04.610
Gonda, just because you say so doesn’t…

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:06.240
Very well, I accept your challenge.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:07.340
Yuuya!

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:10.160
A one-on-one challenge. Come here.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:10.920
Yuuya…

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:12.750
You guys, don’t follow.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:25.650
Oh, there he is!

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:26.930
Nozomu-kun!

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:30.690
What’s the matter?
We were worried earlier.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:32.710
Ah, yes.

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:35.400
Is something the matter?

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:44.840
Yuuya, where’s Gonda?

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.750
Gonda-san!

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:50.700
Yuuya, you…

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:53.380
I’ve been doing Aikido for a long time.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:55.300
What’s the matter?

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:57.630
Oh, sorry.

00:10:57.910 --> 00:10:59.220
We finally found you.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:02.860
Kaoruko-chan, Sumireko-chan and the Sakurazukis,

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:04.430
why don’t we get something warm to drink?

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:06.430
Yes, that sounds good.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.430
Nozomu-kun, will you join us?

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:13.460
I’ll be joining you later. Go on ahead.

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:23.090
Stand back!

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:27.490
Damn it all!

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:29.010
Gonda-san.

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:32.370
Leave me alone.

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:46.180
Umm…

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:49.180
Are you okay?
Are you injured anywhere?

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:51.940
I’m hurt in every possible place.

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:55.860
This is so uncool, getting thrown after trying to hit him.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:58.360
It seems he’s been doing Aikido.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:02.980
I see. He seems very smart, and he’s very strong.

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:04.960
He’s completely different from me.

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:06.370
Oh no.

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:09.150
It’s all right, I understand.

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:13.370
I didn’t even believe myself to be a match for the Ichijous.

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:15.540
Well, about that…

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:19.210
But my feelings towards the Ichijous will not lose to anyone.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:20.670
I don’t intend to lose to anyone in that respect.

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:27.440
Their smiles… I’ll do anything to defend those smiles.

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:32.280
I’ll fight anyone, even if I get severely beat up! I’ll fight as many times as it takes.

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:33.390
Gonda.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:39.400
They’re so bright… just being able to see those smiles is enough.

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:41.890
I’m fine with just that.

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:44.320
I’m very happy.

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:55.000
Gonda. Compared to him, I’m just…

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:01.150
Someday we can go into space.

00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:04.160
I wonder when that’ll be.

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:05.430
He’s late.

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:06.210
Yes.

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:13.950
Nozomu-kun! Over here!

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:14.520
Over here! Over here!

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:17.350
I’m sorry I’m late.

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:19.750
Nozomu-kun, please sit between us.

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:24.610
What would you like to drink? Cocoa?

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.210
Or how about juice?

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:27.280
I’ll be fine with coffee.

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:30.530
Welcome.

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:32.530
One coffee, please.

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:33.880
Certainly.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:40.880
Yuuya-kun was just telling us about the International Space Station.

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:42.840
Ah, yes.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:47.590
If the conditions are right, it can be seen with the naked eye. Quite surprisingly.

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:52.210
It’s still being built, but it’ll be as big as a soccer stadium when it’s finished.

00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:53.080
Yup.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:56.570
Kaoruko-chan seems to be
enjoying herself.

00:13:56.570 --> 00:13:59.230
As I suspected,
Kaoruko-chan is with Yuuya.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:01.010
Sorry for the wait.

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:05.590
Please pass the sugar, Kira-chan.

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:06.770
Okay.

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:09.050
Here you go.

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:15.820
Nozomu-kun, your coffee’s getting cold.

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:16.750
Oh?

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:20.210
Thank you, Kira-chan.

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:25.880
Um, I’m Yura…

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:28.860
Oh sorry!
I called you Kira-chan, Yura-chan…

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:29.940
It’s fine.

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:31.760
It’s no problem at all.

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:37.380
Thanks for today, Nozomu-kun.

00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:38.480
It was a lot of fun.

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:41.190
Um, about earlier…

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:43.890
We were happy to
visit the temple with you.

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:46.700
And all three of us can go to the same high school.

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:52.680
See you again soon.

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:03.290
It’s because I’m not being forthright.

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:05.950
I may have hurt Kira-chan and Yura-chan.

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:09.110
I’m such a… I’m such a…

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:15.040
He got us mixed up.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:15.890
Yes.

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:19.890
Nozomu-kun isn’t the same as usual.

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:23.900
He’s been a little absent-minded or just zoning out today.

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:27.400
Come to think of it, at the Christmas party too.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:31.060
I guess Nozomu-kun has another girl that he likes.

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:31.920
Yes…

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:01.390
I’m such a…

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:03.340
Onii-chan, telephone!

00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:06.150
It’s from your father in Hawaii!

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.380
Yes.

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:09.620
Nozomu, Happy New Year.

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:13.920
Ah, I see, it just turned
New Year’s in Hawaii.

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:16.660
What’s the matter?
You don’t seem too happy.

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:20.540
Oh, I’m just reflecting on things.

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:23.850
Happy New Year, Father.
How are things over there?

00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:26.630
It’s the best. And most of all, the stars are beautiful.

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.020
I see.

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:31.930
It’s great here. How about it?
Why don’t you come out here now?

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:42.150
It seems the Sakurazuki sisters are absent today.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:44.120
Yeah.

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:54.550
Kenmochi-san.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:57.620
Is that so?

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:59.060
The master is going away on business?

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:01.520
Yes, and taking the girls with him.

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:03.010
I see, and so you want…

00:17:03.010 --> 00:17:10.050
Yes. The Misses seem attached to you, Futami-san, and I am well aware of this.

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:11.590
O-oh.

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:16.680
As their companion, I know how much they admire and respect you.

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:18.680
I see.

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:21.440
Since that summer at the chateau,

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:27.000
the girls seem to be very happy every day,
and that makes me happy.

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:31.060
Lately, however, they do not seem to be all that happy,

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:33.280
and now with the master moving away…

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:38.070
While I do not know the details,

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:42.200
I do know that the girls are worrying about you, Futami-san.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:48.630
Kira-sama and Yura-sama wonder if your feelings are in a different place.

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:57.240
So what are the Misses to you?

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:00.720
Oh no, I… that’s…

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:07.730
This is my personal request: please make up your mind clearly.

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:09.380
I’m begging you.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.830
Everyone, I’m sure you know...

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:27.220
Even when the third semester began after winter break,

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:27.610
...what it means to “see the world.”

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:30.760
Kira-chan and Yura-chan were still absent from school.

00:18:27.610 --> 00:18:29.760
Many different cultures and foods…

00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:46.100
Kira-chan, how is it?

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:48.850
Yes, I’m almost done with this reference book.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.000
I’m also done with most of it.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.730
I want to go back to school soon.

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:55.980
Yes, Kenmochi-san is overreacting.

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:58.630
Just over a little fever and he said,

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:01.670
“Your body is more important than the school exams.”

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:03.790
I want to go back soon.

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:05.000
Yes, soon.

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:08.120
I want to see Nozomu-kun!

00:19:08.990 --> 00:19:10.870
We haven’t seen him in a while.

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:13.290
I wonder how Nozomu-kun is doing.

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:22.300
Yura-chan, you’re not worried about it anymore?

00:19:22.790 --> 00:19:28.810
Eh? Yeah, my affections for Nozomu-kun aren’t going to change.

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:30.710
Yes, that’s true.

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:36.570
He may be in love with someone else, but I still love Nozomu-kun.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:40.580
My feelings have finally reached that resolution.

00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:41.740
Yes.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:45.280
Next time, let’s ask Kenmochi-san:

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:48.370
“Can we go back to school?”

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:50.290
Yes, that sounds good.

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:07.480
I wonder which one is Yura-chan and Kira-chan’s room.

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:13.900
Regardless, I have to see them and talk to them.

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:16.940
Honestly tell them my feelings…
honestly…

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:22.120
But can I say it?

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:25.140
Even I don’t know my own feelings.

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:27.480
But in front of Kira-chan and Yura-chan…

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:31.160
Please make up your mind clearly.

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:49.760
We’re off!

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:57.290
Today, we’ll be going to school.

00:20:57.290 --> 00:21:00.650
We’re tired of staying in the house,
so we’ll go to school.

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:06.200
Misses, both of you will never be going back to Souai Middle School.

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:07.730
Eh?

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:10.870
Oh stop it, Kenmochi-san,
what are you talking about?

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:13.710
Never again – now that’s just a lie.

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:15.460
It is not a lie.

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:18.570
I have been contacted by the master and you’ll be transferred

00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:20.850
...back to your old middle school.

00:21:20.850 --> 00:21:23.210
The arrangements are to be made immediately.

00:21:24.680 --> 00:21:28.930
The master is worried about the condition of his Misses,

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:31.640
and I assume you have no objections.

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:35.020
This is all for your sake, Misses.

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:38.050
Transfer?

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
dokomademo tsuzuku sora

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Oh, the sky that continues no matter where you go…

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
daisuki na kono machi de

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
In this town that I love…

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.010
takusan no omoide to, hora,

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.010
With all our memories, now look!

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:16.020
onaji dake hohoende

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:16.020
We are smiling the same way

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:26.700
itsudemo kimi no tonari ni iyoutoshiteru no wa

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:26.700
To always be trying to be besides you…

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
mukashi kara no kuse datte omotteru kedo

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
…is, I believe, a bad habit I’ve had for a long time

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
“mata ashita” tte te wo furu toki ni wa

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
When we wave our hands saying “see you tomorrow,”

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
sukoshi dake samishii kigasuru yo

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
I realize that I’m feeling a little lonely at that moment

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
tooku naru kimi no senaka mitsumete

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
Staring at your back that is getting further away,

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
nandaka, fushigi na kimochi

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
For some reason, a mysterious feeling…

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
kono mune ni hirogatte yuku

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
…is spreading through this heart of mine

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:12.810
Good afternoon! It’s me, Keisuke.

00:23:12.810 --> 00:23:14.650
It’ll be Valentine’s Day soon.

00:23:14.650 --> 00:23:18.960
I’ve been calling out here and there, so I’m bound to get a lot of chocolate.

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:20.960
But Nozomu likely won’t.

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:23.690
Next Time – Valentine Panic!
